    "name": "Chamoli Himalayan Gorge (Uttarakhand Flash Flood)",
    "region": "Rishi Ganga / Dhauliganga Valley, Joshimath, Chamoli District",
    "state": "Uttarakhand",
    "description": "Steep V-shaped Himalayan gorge prone to flash floods and glacial lake outbursts. High mountain walls block low-elevation NavIC satellites below 25-35 degrees, causing acute 3-satellite degradation and high GDOP (>12) for valley-floor NDRF rescue teams.",
